From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:15:12 -0400
Subject: sidebar: density presets and one text-size step

The sidebar's layout constants read a process-wide preset (Comfortable,
the measured Arc match and the feature params; Compact 36/40/16/8; Dense
30/34/16/6 for the row, the essentials card, the favicon and the corner
radius) and a text size (12-15, or the label font as it is); a row is never
shorter than its text with the pill's insets. Both are local-state
preferences: SidebarDensity fills the metrics at the first window and on
every change, and a change re-lays out every window through a theme
change (the fonts, in each row's UpdateColors) and a toolbar-size change
(the heights). Two dropdowns in chrome://settings/stedding under the width
slider, and three bar actions (docs/features/sidebar.md Y1-Y5).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-27: the Zen mods' compact rows and
font sizes, as one preset and one step.
Removable when: Chromium's vertical tab strip has a density setting.
